From: BedrockOnLinux contributors
Subject: [PATCH] vkd3d: keep the frame latency object ticking while occluded

An occluded Present returns DXGI_STATUS_OCCLUDED before it enqueues
anything, so the present callback that releases the frame latency waitable
object never runs. An application which created its swapchain with
DXGI_SWAP_CHAIN_FLAG_FRAME_LATENCY_WAITABLE_OBJECT waits on that object
before every frame, so the first occluded present stops its render loop for
good.

Under Wine that turns into a permanent hang rather than a paused frame. The
window manager iconifying the window is what makes the surface report a zero
maximum image extent in the first place (win32u derives it from the Win32
client rect, which a minimized window reports as empty), and the blocked
render loop no longer pumps messages, so Wine cannot deliver the restore
that would give the window its client rect back. The occlusion can then
never clear: the window stays black and unresponsive until the process is
killed.

Release the waitable object on the occluded path, mirroring what the
present-wait worker does for a retired present, so the render loop keeps
running while occluded and observes the window coming back.

diff --git a/libs/vkd3d/swapchain.c b/libs/vkd3d/swapchain.c
index 8dd2cc10fb2..3e95f7644dd 100644
--- a/libs/vkd3d/swapchain.c
+++ b/libs/vkd3d/swapchain.c
@@ -1130,7 +1130,20 @@
     (void)pPresentParameters;
 
     if (dxgi_vk_swap_chain_present_is_occluded(chain))
+    {
+        /* An application using a waitable swapchain blocks on the frame
+         * latency object before every frame, and only the present callback
+         * below ever releases it. Returning here without releasing it stops
+         * such a render loop for good: the window then stops pumping
+         * messages, the window manager can no longer deliver the restore
+         * that would clear the occlusion, and the application hangs with a
+         * black window until it is killed. Keep the object ticking so the
+         * loop survives being occluded and observes the change.
+         * Releasing an already full semaphore fails harmlessly. */
+        if (vkd3d_native_sync_handle_is_valid(chain->frame_latency_event))
+            vkd3d_native_sync_handle_release(chain->frame_latency_event, 1);
         return DXGI_STATUS_OCCLUDED;
+    }
     if (PresentFlags & DXGI_PRESENT_TEST)
         return S_OK;
 
